---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { baseUrl } from '../../utils/base.ts';
---

<Layout
  title="Roadmap - UOMP"
  description="What UOMP is building next: make the CLI consent loop usable first, then validate MCP clients and package the CLI. Progress is measured by retained users, not shipped features."
  lang="en"
  switchHref={`${baseUrl}roadmap/`}
>
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Roadmap</h1>
      <p>We measure progress by retained users, not shipped features.</p>

      <div class="roadmap">
        <div class="note">
          <strong>Current focus:</strong> make the CLI loop usable — import Obsidian/Markdown, grant for 30 minutes, audit, revoke. MCP client validation and packaged CLI come next.
        </div>

        <h2>Milestone 1: The authorization loop <span class="status status-done">Done</span></h2>
        <ul class="roadmap-list">
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Publish UOMP-Draft-00 specification</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Local SQLite store with CSV/JSON import</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span><code>uom.json</code> manifests with tag, key, and field scopes</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>EdDSA capability tokens, 30-minute default</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Auth Service + Memory Guard with read-only enforcement</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Admin token required for session create, grant, and revoke</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span><code>revoke</code> and <code>close</code> enforced on the next request</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Audit log for every access decision</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>CLI: <code>import</code> / <code>connect</code> / <code>authorize</code> / <code>serve</code> / <code>sessions</code> / <code>revoke</code> / <code>audit</code></li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Markdown / Obsidian folder import with path-derived scopes and <code>--dry-run</code></li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span><code>authorize</code> writes a 0600 session env file and does not print the JWT by default</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>One-command install script (<code>install.sh</code>, source build)</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>stdio MCP server (<code>list_memory</code> / <code>search_memory</code> / <code>read_memory</code>, experimental)</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>TypeScript SDK (<code>UompClient</code>)</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Example agents: calendar and stock analyst</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Milestone 2: The first real-user workflow <span class="status status-current">In progress</span></h2>
        <ul class="roadmap-list">
          <li><span class="status status-next">Next</span>Claude Desktop / Cursor end-to-end validation</li>
          <li><span class="status status-next">Next</span>Packaged CLI release (npm or a standalone binary) without a local build</li>
          <li><span class="status status-next">Next</span>Audit timeline: agent, scope, time, allowed or denied</li>
          <li><span class="status status-next">Next</span>Python SDK</li>
          <li><span class="status status-next">Next</span>10 design partners using their own data</li>
          <li><span class="status status-next">Next</span>Target: first authorized read under 5 minutes</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Milestone 3: After retention is proven <span class="status status-future">Planned</span></h2>
        <ul class="roadmap-list">
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>Second connector (Notion, plain folders, or an existing memory vendor)</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>Team policies, shared scopes, and SSO</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>Hosted relay and multi-device sync</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>Audit export</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>Write workflows with staging and approval</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Research &amp; preview <span class="status status-future">Not scheduled</span></h2>
        <ul class="roadmap-list">
          <li><span class="status status-future">Research</span>FHE (homomorphic encryption)</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Research</span>On-chain audit</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Preview</span>Remote Gateway deployment</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Preview</span>S3 / IPFS storage backends</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Preview</span>Agent registry / marketplace</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These remain in the repository and design docs. They are not on the critical path, and they will not delay the first retained-user workflow.
        </p>

        <h2>How we will know it worked</h2>
        <div class="metric-grid">
          <div class="metric"><strong>10</strong><span>design partners using their own data</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>3+</strong><span>agents connected per user</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>3+</strong><span>uses per week for 4 consecutive weeks</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>&lt;5 min</strong><span>from install to first authorized read</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>≥50%</strong><span>of users revoke a session — control must be felt</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>
          If these numbers do not hold, we change the workflow, not the feature list.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-btns" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <a href={`${baseUrl}en/try/`} class="btn-h1" style="background:#8B5CF6">Try today's loop →</a>
        <a href={`${baseUrl}en/spec/`} class="btn-h1">Read the spec →</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/0xSynapse/uomp-core" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-h2">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
